ets are ordered reversely, so stronger conditions are tree extensions and poset compatibility is tree comparability.","fixed_by":"def-poset-ccc-and-knaster-property","matters_for":["thm-splitting-suslin-tree-poset-square-not-ccc","ex-diamond-suslin-ccc-square"]},{"convention":"Partition arrows quantify one fixed finite arity before the coloring; the target is cardinality, colors are nonzero, and the zero-arity convention is explicit.","fixed_by":"def-partition-arrow-notation","matters_for":["thm-infinite-ramsey-finite-colors","lem-erdos-rado-pattern-closure-and-end-homogeneity","thm-general-cardinal-erdos-rado"]},{"convention":"DC quantifies only over nonempty carriers and serial relations; its sequences start at zero, and the prescribed-start form is a separate equivalent principle.","fixed_by":"def-serial-relation-dependent-choice-principle-over-zf","matters_for":["lem-prescribed-start-and-starting-point-free-serial-choice-are-equivalent-in-zf","thm-serial-dependent-choice-implies-complete-metric-baire-over-zf","thm-complete-metric-baire-principle-implies-dependent-choice-over-zf"]},{"convention":"CM-Baire quantifies over omega-indexed open dense families, uses ambient-space meagreness, and includes the empty metric space.","fixed_by":"def-complete-metric-baire-principle-over-zf","matters_for":["lem-open-dense-and-closed-nowhere-dense-baire-forms-are-equivalent-in-zf","thm-serial-dependent-choice-implies-complete-metric-baire-over-zf","thm-dependent-choice-is-equivalent-to-complete-metric-baire-over-zf"]},{"convention":"The well-ordered-language completeness, Löwenheim–Skolem, tree-construction, delta-system, diamond, and partition claims that state ZFC explicitly use AC; countable-language completeness and compactness are separately stated in classical ZF.","fixed_by":"rem-first-order-choice-strength-boundary","matters_for":["thm-well-ordered-language-henkin-completeness","thm-upward-lowenheim-skolem-with-choice","thm-special-aronszajn-tree-construction","thm-diamond-constructs-normal-suslin-tree","thm-general-cardinal-erdos-rado"]}],"load_bearing":[{"id":"thm-countable-lindenbaum-henkin-completion","statement":"In classical ZF, given an explicitly countable signature and a consistent sentence theory, there is a countable constant expansion and a consistent, deductively closed, syntactically complete Henkin sentence theory extending it.","used_by":["thm-countable-first-order-completeness"]},{"id":"thm-henkin-closed-term-truth-lemma","statement":"For the closed-term quotient of a complete consistent Henkin theory, satisfaction of a formula under closed-term representatives is equivalent to membership of the corresponding simultaneous closed instance in the theory.","used_by":["thm-countable-first-order-completeness","thm-well-ordered-language-henkin-completeness"]},{"id":"thm-countable-first-order-completeness","statement":"In classical ZF, every consistent sentence theory in an explicitly countable set language has a nonempty model whose carrier injects into omega, and semantic consequence equals derivability for sentences.","used_by":["thm-countable-first-order-compactness","thm-nonstandard-natural-number-model-exists","cor-countable-los-vaught-test","fs-categorical-first-order-zf"]},{"id":"lem-bounded-rational-tree-limit-extension","statement":"A countable rationally labelled tree at a nonzero countable limit height satisfying the stated bounded-extension and infinitely-many-small-successors invariants can be extended by a countable limit level while preserving them and normality.","used_by":["thm-special-aronszajn-tree-construction"]},{"id":"thm-special-aronszajn-tree-construction","statement":"In ZFC there exists a normal splitting special Aronszajn tree.","used_by":["fs-every-omega-one-tree-has-a-cofinal-branch"]},{"id":"thm-diamond-constructs-normal-suslin-tree","statement":"In ZFC, diamond implies that a normal splitting Suslin tree exists, constructible on omega_1 with singleton root and countably infinite positive levels.","used_by":["ex-diamond-suslin-ccc-square"]},{"id":"lem-erdos-rado-pattern-closure-and-end-homogeneity","statement":"For the stated cardinals and finite d, every coloring of [((2^mu)^+)]^(d+1) admits a mu^+-long sequence and an outside point with equal patterns on each d-subset of earlier sequence elements.","used_by":["thm-general-cardinal-erdos-rado"]},{"id":"lem-discrete-sequence-spaces-are-complete-in-zf","statement":"For nonempty A, the reciprocal first-difference metric on A^omega is a nonempty complete ultrametric space whose finite-prefix cylinders are nonempty clopen basic sets.","used_by":["lem-serial-relation-successor-sets-are-open-dense","thm-complete-metric-baire-principle-implies-dependent-choice-over-zf","ex-blair-sequence-space-for-a-serial-relation"]},{"id":"thm-serial-dependent-choice-implies-complete-metric-baire-over-zf","statement":"Over ZF, DC implies that every complete metric space is Baire for omega-indexed open dense families.","used_by":["thm-dependent-choice-is-equivalent-to-complete-metric-baire-over-zf"]},{"id":"thm-complete-metric-baire-principle-implies-dependent-choice-over-zf","statement":"Over ZF, the complete-metric Baire principle implies both starting-point-free and prescribed-start Dependent Choice.","used_by":["thm-dependent-choice-is-equivalent-to-complete-metric-baire-over-zf","ex-blair-sequence-space-for-a-serial-relation"]}],"published_dependencies":[{"id":"cor-archimedean-reciprocal","used_for":"Shrinking positive metric radii.","opened":true},{"id":"cor-cardinal-absorption","used_for":"Infinite-cardinal size bounds.","opened":true},{"id":"cor-distributive-and-de-morgan-laws-for-indexed-families","used_for":"Baire-form equivalences.","opened":true},{"id":"def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies","used_for":"Relative beth and successor notation.","opened":true},{"id":"def-axiom-of-choice","used_for":"Declared ZFC/AC uses.","opened":true},{"id":"def-axiom-of-extensionality","used_for":"Coded ZF theory.","opened":true},{"id"